C)`-sub-equilibrium tail: the orbit stays above the high floor `v` and\n    its valuation sum never exceeds `m·log₂3 + C` (it ascends or hovers forever). -/\ndef SubEquilibriumTail (x₀ : ℕ) (v : ℕ) (C : ℝ) : Prop :=\n  (∀ m, orbit x₀ m ≥ v) ∧ (∀ m, (valSum x₀ m : ℝ) ≤ m * Real.logb 2 3 + C)\n\n/-! ## The single open input -/\n\n/-- **Pointwise Valuation Theorem (the single open axiom).**\n    No positive odd start admits an infinite high-regime sub-equilibrium tail:\n    no orbit can keep its accelerated valuations averaging below `log₂3` forever"}